[38;2;255;255;255m●[39m I recorded it in HiveMind. The new decision is [1m"Pantry [0m
  [1mstorage: Postgres on the home server"[0m ([38;2;177;185;249mdecision-370866d3-…[39m).
  It's marked as replacing the old SQLite decision
  ([38;2;177;185;249mdecision-456d94e3-…[39m), and the old one's status is now
  [38;2;177;185;249msuperseded[39m.

  The rationale I wrote says:
  - Pantry now has to work from your phone and your laptop, and
    one SQLite file can't be shared between them.
  - Postgres on the home server can be reached from both
    devices.
  - This takes on the cost the SQLite decision avoided: a
    separate database server to run and back up.
  - Postgres still gives transactional writes, which was the
    original reason for moving off the JSON file.

  The new decision's status is [38;2;177;185;249mproposed[39m, the tool's default. I
  didn't mark it accepted.

  The code still uses SQLite ([38;2;177;185;249mpantry.db[39m, from commit [38;2;177;185;249m8443c86[39m). I
  can move the storage layer to Postgres next if you want. For
  that I'd need to know how to connect to your home server.

